  "cues": [
   [
    0.117,
    "Some cells live in an environment that is never isotonic."
   ],
   [
    3.88,
    "Take Paramecium, a single cell living in pond water."
   ],
   [
    7.747,
    "The slide says Paramecium is hypertonic to its pond water."
   ],
   [
    11.771,
    "Put simply, its cytoplasm has more solute than the pond, so the pond water is hypotonic to the cell."
   ],
   [
    18.659,
    "Water keeps flowing in by osmosis."
   ],
   [
    21.549,
    "Left alone, the cell would swell and burst."
   ],
   [
    24.922,
    "Its answer is the contractile vacuole, an organelle that acts as a pump."
   ],
   [
    29.635,
    "It collects the extra water and squeezes it out of the cell, over and over."
   ],
   [
    34.531,
    "This is osmoregulation, the control of solute concentration and water balance."
   ],
   [
    40.339,
    "Hypertonic or hypotonic surroundings create osmotic problems, and osmoregulation is the adaptation for life in them."
   ],
   [
    48.581,
    "How a pump is powered is a story for lesson five."
   ]
  ]
